OL,3,GNEWSAHolidaymaker says visa error
OL,4,Ablocked entry to Italy
OL,5,
OL,6,FA holidaymaker said she believed she
OL,7,Fwas refused entry at the Italian border
OL,8,Fdue to a computer error that recorded
OL,9,Fher as having overstayed a visa.
OL,11,FPaula Pugh, 61, from Swaffham, Norfolk,
OL,12,Ftravelled from Stansted Airport to
OL,13,FCalabria in southern Italy for a
OL,14,Ffive-day holiday to celebrate her
OL,15,Fhusband's birthday in September.
OL,17,FAfter arriving she was told she had
OL,18,Fexceeded her 90-day visa-free allowance
OL,19,Fto the Schengen area and was put on a
OL,20,Freturn flight, but Pugh said this was a
OL,21,Fdatabase error and that she had only
OL,22,Fspent 22 days in the area.
OL,23,APub: 17-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
